  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper reports two gate-based quantum experiments on the Boston Housing regression task: a 9-qubit hybrid QNN using PennyLane default.qubit.tf with AngleEmbedding and StronglyEntanglingLayers, and a photonic continuous-variable hybrid QNN using Strawberry Fields Fock backend with 3 features and CVNeuralNetLayers. Both were trained for 25 epochs with batch size 5, learning rate 0.08, and 1024 shots; the hybrid QNN is reported to perform slightly better than a classical NN, while the photonic model largely failed to learn because of simulation memory limits.",
